  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 2608.03 Period of Suspension",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2608.03 Period of Suspension.\n\n(a) The suspension period for a single violation of RSA 160-C:2, II within a 12-month period shall be a minimum of 10 consecutive days, but no longer than 14 days.\n\n(b) The suspension period for any violation set forth in Saf-C 2608.02 , or a subsequent violation of RSA 160-C:2, II in a 12-month period, shall be a maximum of 5 years.\n\n(c) The length of the suspension period shall correlate directly with:\n\n(1) The seriousness of the offense; and\n\n(2) Whether there are aggravating factors.\n\n(d) For the purposes of (c)(2) above, aggravating factors shall include:\n\n(1) Previous license suspensions pursuant to Saf-C 2608.02;\n\n(2) Previous non-compliance with any laws, rules, or regulations related to fireworks;\n\n(3) Actions which the licensee knew or should have known were contrary to any laws, rules, or regulations related to fireworks; and\n\n(4) Actions by the licensee which create a hazard to public safety.\n\n(e) Notwithstanding any rule to the contrary, any licensee found to be selling permissible fireworks after the person’s license has been suspended pursuant to RSA 160-C:8, and Saf-C 2608.05 below, shall not have the license reinstated for a minimum of one year from the date of the immediate suspension.\n\nSource. #10784, eff 2-13-15",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2600.html"
